## Program Structure

    boot.S          Raspberry Pi boot entry
    main.c          hardware initialization and kernel startup
    kernel.c/h      kernel dispatcher and scheduler control
    task.c/h        task descriptors, task stacks, ready queues
    syscall.c/h     syscall wrapper functions
    syscall_asm.S   SVC, exception vector, context save/restore
    tasks.c/h       FirstUserTask and TestTask
    uart.c/h        UART terminal I/O
    rpi.c/h         Raspberry Pi GPIO setup
    util.c/h        formatting helpers

## Kernel Design

The kernel uses a static task descriptor array and statically allocated task stacks.  
There is no heap allocation.

Each task descriptor stores:

    task id
    parent task id
    priority
    run state
    saved stack pointer
    entry function pointer
    ready queue next pointer

The scheduler uses static priority queues. Lower numeric priority means higher scheduling priority. Tasks at the same priority are scheduled FIFO / round-robin.

